## Module 3: Guardrails
- evidence_mode = true
- if evidence_mode == true:
    - LLM must only include claims, equations, and results from the given text
    - If the LLM cannot find enough information, it must explicitly state such

- Flag missing/empty sections.
- Flag sections <50 words.
- if a section has been flagged the module must instruct the LLM to output a standardized warning explaining why the section was flagged. For example:"section skipped, not enough information available in section to complete summary"

- Mitigate hallucinations: only summarize provided text.
- Chunk long papers into manageable segments.
